# EXAMPLE PROJECT IN THE KIT REPO: no Git LFS here, on purpose.
# The kit's games normally route images, audio, 3D and fonts through Git LFS (see docs/sop/SOP-05-git.md), and your own
# game should. This example's assets are small, and GitHub's "Download ZIP" does not include LFS files by default, so a
# beginner downloading the kit would get pointer files instead of art. Plain git keeps the example working everywhere.

# Text: normalize line endings so Windows and macOS/Linux clones agree; Unity YAML stays text
* text=auto eol=lf
*.unity text eol=lf
*.asset text eol=lf
*.meta  text eol=lf

# Binary files: never touch line endings, never diff as text
*.png  binary
*.gif  binary
*.ogg  binary
*.wav  binary
*.fbx  binary
*.ttf  binary
